Here are some commonly used functions for a multi-layer perceptron (MLP) in C++:

1. sigmoid: The sigmoid function is used as the activation function for the output layer of the MLP. It takes a single input value and returns the output value between 0 and 1.
```c
double sigmoid(double x) {
    return 1.0 / (1.0 + exp(-x));
}
```
2. softmax: The softmax function is used as the activation function for the output layer of the MLP when the output layer has more than one neuron. It takes a vector of input values and returns a vector of output values between 0 and 1, representing the probabilities of each output.
```c
vector<double> softmax(vector<double> x) {
    vector<double> y(x.size());
    for (int i = 0; i < x.size(); i++) {
        y[i] = exp(x[i]);
    }
    return y;
}
```
3. ReLU: The rectified linear unit (ReLU) function is used as the activation function for the hidden layers of the MLP. It takes a single input value and returns the input value if it is positive, and 0 if it is negative.
```c
double ReLU(double x) {
    return (x > 0) ? x : 0;
}
```
4. NAME_1: The hyperbolic tangent (NAME_1) function is also used as the activation function for the hidden layers of the MLP. It takes a single input value and returns the output value between -1 and 1.
```c
double NAME_1(double x) {
    return (x > 0) ? 1.0 / (1.0 + exp(-2.0 * x)) : 1.0 / (1.0 - exp(-2.0 * x));
}
```
