  // Set the time limit for the form in milliseconds (1000 milliseconds = 1 minute)
  const timeLimit = 60000; // 1 minute

  // Get the form element
  const form = document.getElementById("time-limit-form");

  // Add an event listener to the form to trigger the validation
  form.addEventListener("submit", function(event) {
    // Stop the default form submission behavior
    event.preventDefault();

    // Get the current time
    const currentTime = new Date().getTime();

    // Check if the time limit has been exceeded
    if (currentTime - form.lastSubmittedTime > timeLimit) {
      // The time limit has been exceeded, show an error message
      form.classList.add("submitted-error");
      form.lastSubmittedTime = currentTime;
    } else {
      // The time limit has not been exceeded, submit the form
      form.classList.remove("submitted-error");
      form.lastSubmittedTime = currentTime;
      form.submit();
    }
  });
</script>
```
This code sets a time limit of 1 minute (60,000 milliseconds) for the form with the `id` of "time-limit-form". When the form is submitted, the code checks the current time and compares it to the last time the form was submitted. If the time limit has been exceeded, the form will be marked as "submitted-error" and will not be submitted. If the time limit has not been exceeded, the form will be submitted.

