Here is an example of how this can be done:
```
class MyCustomWidget extends StatelessWidget {
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return Provider(
      create: (context) => MySubWidget(),
      child: Column(
        children: [
          // other subwidgets
          Provider.of<MySubWidget>(context, listen: false).subWidget1,
          Provider.of<MySubWidget>(context, listen: false).subWidget2,
        ],
      ),
    );
  }
}
```
In the above example, the MyCustomWidget class is created and it uses the Provider.of method to access the MySubWidget class and create instances of it. The instances are then added to the Column widget as children. The listen: false parameter is passed to the Provider.of method to ensure that the widgets are not rebuilt every time the context changes.

