The `fetchApk` function uses the `fetch` function to make a GET request to the URL where the APK is hosted. When the response is received, we use the `blob` method to get the binary data of the APK and set it as the state of the `apk` variable.

Finally, we use conditional rendering to display a message indicating whether the APK has been downloaded successfully or is still being loaded. We display the binary data of the APK in a `pre` tag if it has been downloaded successfully.

