let parsedArgs = {};

// Loop through the args array and parse each one
for (let i = 0; i < argsArray.length; i++) {
  // Check if the current arg is a flag
  if (argsArray[i][0] === "-") {
    // If it is a flag, add it to the parsed flags object
    parsedArgs[argsArray[i].substring(1)] = true;
  } else {
    // If it is not a flag, add it to the parsed args object as a value
    parsedArgs["text"] = argsArray[i];
  }
}

// Print the parsed args
console.log(parsedArgs);
```
This script first splits the args string into an array of individual args, then loops through the array and parses each arg. If an arg starts with a "-" character, it is treated as a flag and added to an object as a property with the flag name as the key and `true` as the value. If an arg does not start with a "-" character, it is treated as a value and added to an object as a property with the key "text" and the value of the arg. Finally, the script prints the parsed args.

