This loop starts at the highest bit of a binary number and iterates backwards to the lowest bit, with the index `i` representing the value of the binary number at each iteration. The `num_bits` variable determines the number of bits in the binary number, and the loop continues until `i` is greater than 0.

You can use this loop to perform operations on binary numbers in reverse order, such as finding the largest or smallest bit in a binary number.

