```
class Queue:
    def __init__(self):
        self.q1 = []
        self.q2 = []

    def enqueue(self, element):
        if len(self.q1) == 0:
            self.q2.append(element)
        else:
            self.q1.append(element)

    def dequeue(self):
        if len(self.q1) != 0:
            return self.q1.pop()
        else:
            return self.q2.pop()

    def peek(self):
        return self.q1[-1] if len(self.q1) > 0 else self.q2[-1]

    def get_size(self):
        return len(self.q1) + len(self.q2)

```

This class has two attributes: `` q1 `` and `` q2 ``, which are lists of elements that can be used as a queue. The `` enqueue() `` method adds an element to the queue if the current queue is empty, otherwise it adds the element to the queue. The `` dequeue() `` method removes and returns the element at the front of the queue if it exists, otherwise it removes and returns the element at the front of the other queue. The `` peek() `` method returns the element at the back of the queue if it exists, otherwise it returns the element at the back of the other queue. The `` get_size() `` method returns the sum of the size of the two queues.

