function toggleDisabled(node) {
  if (node.disabled) {
    node.disabled = false;
    if (node.children.length > 0) {
      for (let i = 0; i < node.children.length; i++) {
        toggleDisabled(node.children[i]);
      }
    }
  }
}
```
In this implementation, we define a function `toggleDisabled` that takes a `node` object as input and recursively traverses the tree to find all its descendants. For each node, we check whether its `disabled` prop is true. If it is, we set it to false and recursively call the function for each of its children.

