Here is a python function to get all prime numbers up to a given number n:
```python
def is_prime(n):
    for i in range(2,int(math.sqrt(n))+1):
        if (n%i) == 0:
            return False
    return True
```

It uses the Sieve of Eratosthenes to find all prime numbers up to the square root of the input number.

